+## 2026-09-05 05:25Z — CORRECTION 7: my provenance work was redundant, and the headline is now dark
+
+**The dashboard's generalization line went from "5 level(s) across 9 game(s)" to
+"measured rows excluded from headline: 9 provenance rejection(s)".** Cause found before blaming
+my own change, and it is not mine: the conductor shipped
+`971f63ff70 [conductor] ARC evaluation hardware and context provenance contract` in milestone
+.614.
+
+**CORRECTION 7, mine to own.** Last hour I implemented REQ-ARC-WMTE-7021 and 7022 —
+`solve_provenance` and a `run_envelope` on eval runs — and reported them as delivered. The
+conductor built the same idea independently, within hours, and **its version is a superset that
+mine does not feed**:
+
+- Mine stamps `solve_provenance` at the DOCUMENT level. The conductor's validator,
+  `validate_arc_evaluation_row`, checks it **per per-game ROW**, and additionally requires a
+  nested `arc_eval_provenance` record that agrees with it. My document stamp satisfies neither
+  clause.
+- My `run_envelope` records n_ctx, requested and held GPUs, model path and hostname. The
+  conductor's record requires `gpu_uuid`, `gpu_model`, `cuda_device`, `model_repository`,
+  `model_filename`, `model_hash`, `n_ctx`, `server_binary`, `server_binary_hash`,
+  `server_command_hash`, `endpoint`, `port`, and a lease id, hash and issue time. A strict
+  superset.
+
+The conductor's `scripts/arc_leaderboard_eval.py` already stamps the row (line ~1225) and builds
+the record (line ~1303). My document-level stamp at line ~1394 sits beside it doing nothing. Two
+implementations of one contract, hours apart, and the redundant one is mine. **Not deleted here:**
+the conductor is actively editing that file this milestone and HEAD is one of its checkpoints, so
+removing my lines now is a collision risk rather than a tidy-up. Flagged for the operator.
+
+**The measurement is intact; only the reporting is dark.** Read directly from
+`generalization_levels()`: `measured: True, levels: 5, games: 9`, and
+`headline_eligible: False` with 9 rejections. The five levels are still measured. The dashboard
+declines to show them.
+
+**It cannot self-heal.** `headline_eligible = all(provenance_decisions.values())` is
+all-or-nothing, and **0 of 27 existing per-game rows carry `arc_eval_provenance`** — the field
+did not exist when they were written. So the line stays dark until every tracked game is re-run
+under the new contract. On the measured cost of a single deep run, that is many GPU-hours.
+
+**OPERATOR DECISION 9.** Whether an unverifiable row should suppress the headline or qualify it.
+Suppressing is defensible and strict. The alternative is to report "5 levels, 9 rows unverified",
+which keeps a measured result visible while naming exactly what is unproven. As written, a
+correct measurement reads as no measurement, and that is the shape a reader misreads as a
+regression — it read that way to me first.
+
+**OPERATOR DECISION 10.** Whether to remove my redundant REQ-7021/7022 stamps, or to keep the
+`run_envelope` for the fields the conductor's record omits (hostname, `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`, and
+the requested-versus-held distinction, which the conductor's `cuda_device` alone does not carry).
+
